.TH QFW-SITE.YAML 5 "August 2026" "QFw 0.1.0" "QFw File Formats"
.SH NAME
qfw-site.yaml \- define QFw installation and site-service settings
.SH DESCRIPTION
The QFw site configuration describes installed paths and services shared by
applications. It is YAML with top-level
.BR install ,
.BR directory-service ,
.BR service ,
and
.B qpm
mappings.
.PP
The default installed path is
.IR prefix/share/qfw/config/site.yaml .
Administrators normally provide a protected site-specific file and select it
through
.B QFW_SITE_CONFIG
or a command's
.B --site-config
option.
.SH INSTALL MAPPING
.TP
.B qfw-prefix
QFw installation prefix. The value
.B ${QFW_PREFIX}
expands from the environment established by
.BR qfw-activate (1).
.TP
.B defw-prefix
DEFw installation prefix. The value
.B ${DEFW_PREFIX}
expands from the activated environment. Referencing an unset or empty
environment variable is a configuration error.
.SH DIRECTORY-SERVICE MAPPING
The
.B directory-service
mapping describes the long-running site directory service.
.TP
.B name
DEFw name of the directory service.
.TP
.B listen-port
Control port opened on the node selected by
.BR qfw-dir-svc (1).
.TP
.B connection-file
Stable, client-readable JSON record written by
.BR qfw-dir-svc (1).
The path must be visible at the same location on service and application
nodes when the service host is selected dynamically.
.TP
.B endpoint
Optional permanent client endpoint in
.I host:port
form. Use this instead of
.B connection-file
only when the site provides a stable hostname or address.
.TP
.B connect-timeout-seconds
Maximum time to wait for directory readiness.
.SH SERVICE MAPPING
.TP
.B manifest
Path to a service manifest described by
.BR qfw-services.yaml (5).
Relative paths are resolved from the site configuration directory.
.TP
.B device-access-config
Path to protected device and credential bindings. Runtime state and client
environment files do not copy credential values from this file.
.SH QPM MAPPING
The
.B qpm
mapping contains settings shared by QPM implementations. The
.B completion-queues.retention
mapping controls completion record lifetime, terminal reservation retention,
record limits, byte limits, and purge frequency.
.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
install:
  qfw-prefix: /opt/qfw
  defw-prefix: /opt/qfw

directory-service:
  name: qfw-site-dirsvc
  listen-port: 8090
  connect-timeout-seconds: 120
  connection-file: /shared/qfw/services/directory-service.json

service:
  manifest: /etc/openqse/qfw/services.yaml
  device-access-config: /etc/openqse/qfw/device-access.yaml
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR qfw-service-plane (1),
.BR qfw-runtime.yaml (5),
.BR qfw-services.yaml (5),
.BR qfw-service-plane (7)
